---
import BaseHead from '../../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE } from '../../consts';
import '../../styles/academic-project.css';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={`Movie Recommendation Application | ${SITE_TITLE}`} description="A computer science capstone combining a natural-language interface, the OpenAI API, and PostgreSQL for movie preferences and recommendation retrieval." />
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main class="academic-project">
			<div class="project-header">
				<p class="project-context">Computer Science Capstone · August - December 2024</p>
				<h1>Movie Recommendation Application</h1>
				<p class="subtitle">A full-stack Python application connecting natural-language requests to user profiles, movie preferences, and recommendation retrieval in PostgreSQL.</p>
				<p class="project-context">Advanced Data Management Technologies Laboratory · University of Pittsburgh</p>
				<ul class="technologies" aria-label="Technologies used">
					<li>Python</li>
					<li>Streamlit</li>
					<li>OpenAI API</li>
					<li>PostgreSQL</li>
					<li>SQL</li>
				</ul>
			</div>

			<section class="prose glass-card">
				<h2>Project Overview</h2>
				<p>I developed the application layer supporting a movie recommendation system, integrating a Streamlit interface, Python application logic, the OpenAI API, and PostgreSQL. Users could provide profile information and movie preferences conversationally, with the application translating their requests into database operations and returning natural-language responses.</p>
				<p>The core engineering challenge was coordinating a multi-step conversation with persistent data: interpreting flexible user input, storing the relevant information, and retrieving it for subsequent interactions.</p>
			</section>

			<section class="prose glass-card">
				<h2>My Responsibilities</h2>
				<p>I built the user interface and the integrations connecting it to the language model and database. My scope covered the conversation flow, profile and preference storage, and the request-to-SQL pipeline supporting preference updates and recommendation retrieval.</p>
				<p>The interface collected names, genre preferences, and movie ratings. I integrated language-model processing to extract relevant information from short answers or full sentences and prompt users again when their responses did not address the question.</p>
				<p>I implemented PostgreSQL storage and retrieval so the application could recognize returning profiles and reuse saved preferences without repeating the initial rating collection.</p>
			</section>

			<section class="prose glass-card">
				<h2>How It Works</h2>
				<ol class="pipeline">
					<li><strong>Start with a conversation.</strong> The user provides profile information, shares movie preferences, or requests recommendations through the natural-language interface.</li>
					<li><strong>Translate the request.</strong> Python application logic and the OpenAI API interpret the input and translate the relevant request into SQL.</li>
					<li><strong>Work with stored data.</strong> PostgreSQL stores or retrieves profile and preference information, supporting preference updates and recommendation retrieval.</li>
					<li><strong>Respond in natural language.</strong> Database query results are translated into a readable response and returned through the interface.</li>
				</ol>
			</section>

			<section class="prose glass-card">
				<h2>Engineering Decisions</h2>
				<p><strong>Consolidating the application in Python.</strong> The initial React and Flask structure required repeated coordination between separate frontend and backend layers during the conversation. I moved the interface to Streamlit and reorganized the existing Python code, bringing conversation handling, API calls, and database operations into a simpler application structure.</p>
				<p><strong>Separating conversational input from stored information.</strong> Language-model processing extracted the information needed at each step, allowing flexible phrasing while preserving structured profile and preference data in PostgreSQL.</p>
				<p><strong>Supporting recommendation integration.</strong> I structured the application to accommodate recommendation functionality through an API, keeping the interface and data-management work adaptable as the broader system evolved.</p>
			</section>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
